I think what Carlos is asking is what to do with fit stats and  
descriptives.  I know Mplus averages fit statistics but I have not  
seen any justification for this behavior in anything published.  Is it  
OK to average R squares, Chi-square tests, CFI, TLI, SRMR, etc. ?

The descriptives question is strait forward for means, percentiles  
(average) variances, standard errors (the more complicated rule) but  
tricky for minimums and maximums, skewness, krutosis, etc.  Not sure  
what to do with these either.  Maybe averaging them is OK.  For  
minimum/maximum I would use minimum/maximum without imputation.

L

