Hello Beiting,

There was a small bug in the code that caused this behavior. It
happened when one or more of the imputation chains ended up with a
non-invertible covariance matrix. This often happens when there are
highly collinear variables in the dataset (e.g. the same variable
twice). I just uploaded a new version of Amelia (1.1-32) that fixes
the bug. You can install this version by typing the following at the R
prompt:

install.packages("Amelia", repos="http://gking.harvard.edu")

You should see that now a warning message will be issued about the colliearity.

good luck,
matt.

